# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# telegram-ai-cli: live account material. Never commit any of this.
#
# A Telethon .session file holds a plaintext 256-bit MTProto auth key. Anyone
# who obtains it controls the account until the session is revoked by hand, so
# these patterns are a hard requirement, not tidiness.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anchored to the repo root with a leading slash. Unanchored, `accounts/`
# also matched the telegram_ai_cli/accounts/ source package and silently kept
# the entire module out of the repository.
/sessions/
/accounts/
/tdata/
/tdatas/
*.session
*.session-journal
*.session-wal
*.session-shm
*.session.lock
*.api.json
*.string

# Local state: plan database, audit log, downloaded media, secret key material.
/state/
/downloads/
/audit/
*.audit.jsonl
/secret.key

# The local message archive (`tg-ai archive sync`). Other people's messages,
# stored unencrypted by design — see docs/configuration.md. It must never reach
# a commit, so the WAL sidecars are named too: they hold committed rows that the
# main file does not yet.
archive.sqlite3
archive.sqlite3-wal
archive.sqlite3-shm
archive.sqlite3-journal
*.archive.sqlite3

# Local config may carry api_id/api_hash and proxy credentials.
tgai.yaml
config/tgai.yaml
.env.*
!.env.example

# Private denylist for test_no_private_data (kept outside the repo by design).
private-denylist.txt
